From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 23:25:54 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/5] Shield review fixes: no task shield outlives its phase,
 follow and escape keep the sprint, and the hand-policy nits

MAJOR 1: a shield a task raised for itself (CombatTask BLOCK, CreeperDefenseTask SHIELD) is lowered by ShieldGuard on its next tick as soon as the active task is not in that phase (ended, paused, replaced: a combat_timeout in BLOCK, a resume of the paused follow or mine); the combat timeout also lowers it itself; the safety net's stand-down and a failed guard tick lower a guard-tracked shield too. New GameTest: a fight ending with its shield up (fail combat_timeout in BLOCK) leaves nothing up and the paused follow resumes.

MAJOR 2 (RULES win over the spec: followers and escorts always sprint while hostiles are aggroed, a warden flight sprints): a FollowTask blocks only projectiles already in flight (a short hold), no pre-emptive hold against a drawing or loaded shooter, a charging guardian beam or a fuse; EvadeTask owns the hands. Test h premise changed accordingly: the follower passes a skeleton that keeps drawing at it and must NOT raise; the skeleton's arrow is blocked with a short raise during which the forward key is at the 0.2 item-use pace and no sprint, the shield comes down within 10 ticks of the block and the follower gets back to its full pace. Test i fires the arrow once the skeleton is noticed (in-flight block with the hotbar switch first). The guardian GameTest is removed: outside follow mode no stable fixture was found (the bot closes in and the beam stops within 3 blocks; a pool rim cuts the line; a rooted bot's view of a guardian at the rim is blocked); the beam decision stays covered by ShieldBlockabilityTest and was seen live earlier (bite applied=false, magic applied). The shooter and guardian scan is now the profile observation radius (what the bot can notice at all) instead of 24.

Nits: a pending heal (EatTask, CombatTask HEAL) is CONSUMING for the hand policy; EatAction refuses a bite while a shield is up and EatTask waits (no budget, no watchdog) instead of dropping the shield; no assess/turn when there is nothing to raise (no shield, retry pending, axe cooldown); GuardTask's raw strafe carries the 0.2 slowdown; BuildAction refuses placing and item-on-block use while a shield is up; ProjectileThreat checks moving, own, blockable, course, then the perception rays; a heard shot uses angle factor 1 even in view (CreatureSenses.heardProjectileShot); an ownerless wither skull is magic 5, a firework rocket without explosions or not shot at an angle deals nothing; more items that take the use (eye of ender, books, boats, lily pad and frogspawn, bundle); the hotbar switch uses slots 0-8 only; AttackEntityTask waits on hands_busy; test a checks the recorded raise cause (shooter_draw, that skeleton); stale comments fixed; dead code removed (ProjectileThreat.mostImminent, ShieldRules.inArc and blockDelayRemaining, which only tests used).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
